#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "391bb8ae-88ba-520c-a5cf-7e2fa5474788" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed in Plain English"}] :question/id #uuid "12d987fd-f966-522d-9370-48f7306930ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-12731" :question/problem "Write down $\\lnot P(x)$ given that\n![](images/ed/ed810318e9b5d6e76b77735530ff9312af66f936d7c8e197d6dd0fb99227dcb8.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n![](images/97/976e6fe9a107732c81210776e49cfe3f68939512c0fad63739e2f59acb17f109.svg) \n\nIn other words, $x$ is smaller than $10.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n![](images/dc/dca132f34f73e2f5987a803e592c1f664cc790ed83ec204205975c401280038c.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198103 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/id #uuid "fcee0d41-9ff9-5f84-b8fe-73bfad36c7bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12732" :question/problem "The shaded region below represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Determine the region that represents the truth set of $\\neg P(x).$ \n\n![](images/cc/cc80d49abe6293acb1325035799dac833a9bcb8f485ed1f785f78c4e1f39b8be.png)" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $\\neg P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{\\neg P} = \\overline{T}_P\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $\\neg P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in $T_p,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/86/86205c3b03c01581677b4fa877dae8c4ca743fe0ac0f1673ef504d548e8c785d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198111 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7943a26b-d4fa-5ce1-bc47-5ea4873fc367" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed Using Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "adacf679-91a6-500f-b13a-18418d851d5b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12883" :question/problem "$\\qquad$ $x \\nleq \\sqrt{2}$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Write down $\\neg P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is not smaller than or equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nThe symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ It is not true that $x$ is not smaller than or equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ *is* *smaller than or equal to* $\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x\\leq \\sqrt{2}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b410a78-f767-5568-ab2b-98dcde5467bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194878} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5af4f-fa18-5a12-9d4b-405238a0c985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194879} {:answer/id #uuid "58d76e8b-1a86-5ffa-acd2-1fa5e4dbcdfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,4,6,8,9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430188} {:answer/id #uuid "a8df4836-12c1-578d-98ab-34cb7a048b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,3,5,7\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430194} {:answer/id #uuid "c4deb8d6-b558-5a44-a9ac-edf5f9c74500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d76e8b-1a86-5ffa-acd2-1fa5e4dbcdfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,4,6,8,9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430188} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dfc675b-4b61-5ea0-9a02-5e53514726dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46ce81ed-7f98-523e-8348-7d75c19c5c70" :question/math-academy-id "q-171685" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of positive integers between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive: \n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x$ is prime" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P},\n$$\n\nThe truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of primes between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{2,3,5,7\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{\\{2,3,5,7\\}} \\\\  & =\\{1,4,6,8,9,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7943a26b-d4fa-5ce1-bc47-5ea4873fc367" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed Using Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1265bd5a-78cd-5b77-952d-2c9a8def8f52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430179} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9859b4-7393-5df1-a3c2-e0b992884a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430197} {:answer/id #uuid "d0984546-b20e-5b16-9c6e-a0f235f5b648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430201} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e38f9b-e8f7-5d70-99cf-388691c482ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x≰\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430202} {:answer/id #uuid "de5c211d-af73-5bd4-ae3e-1c13d8266b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0984546-b20e-5b16-9c6e-a0f235f5b648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430201} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd67b3c-2b82-5f26-85f7-a27a12134ac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f94afce2-6e2a-536a-8567-c4c1dfc21cb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-175313" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x≱\\pi $\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nIn other words, $x$ *is* *greater than or equal to* $\\pi .$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\ge \\pi $"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "391bb8ae-88ba-520c-a5cf-7e2fa5474788" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed in Plain English"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ade7d61-5826-5d6e-8c44-465826c146fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is smaller than $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430183} {:answer/id #uuid "68ae4d49-f3f0-502a-b9d7-38aa0c211660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than or equal to $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430189} {:answer/id #uuid "af5653ad-ac62-587a-bac4-a6048e331507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is equal to $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430195} {:answer/id #uuid "b34e3514-08c0-5818-a19c-8df103450dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not greater than $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430196} {:answer/id #uuid "bad69646-8267-5dda-8461-557726caa010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68ae4d49-f3f0-502a-b9d7-38aa0c211660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than or equal to $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430189} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b10d84a-ed52-5d15-bf1f-79a5856c3da0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0373eae5-d413-558b-aff8-967aba0289ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-175412" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is smaller than $y.$\n\nThe predicate $P(x,y)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is smaller than $y.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$ Therefore, $¬P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "391bb8ae-88ba-520c-a5cf-7e2fa5474788" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed in Plain English"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ec13d9-ba04-5cf2-871e-2d3da08d0af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not greater than $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430182} {:answer/id #uuid "c186e2f7-ceca-5bf5-a121-ec500999054d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430199} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ff3d40-913d-5dda-9c9a-d4a87dacba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is smaller than $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430204} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d99c01-33bd-5bc6-a18e-4cf6f884a4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is not equal to $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430205} {:answer/id #uuid "f26ba7d0-f50d-5e14-abd0-b24c0635b31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than or equal to $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c186e2f7-ceca-5bf5-a121-ec500999054d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is greater than $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430199} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00b0b0b-3141-5bf4-8a83-5d11c6bf823a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33e4bfa0-0240-5076-a3cc-c397d31c6632" :question/math-academy-id "q-175413" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is smaller than or equal to $3.$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is smaller than or equal to $3.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is greater than $3.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f25b9b-3d35-56ca-9327-f8285b1ec334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430180} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0baf9c-dfdb-50b1-8d2c-f2950159bc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430184} {:answer/id #uuid "54737426-e934-5b9e-a7e3-ee8d5c4c5497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430187} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8e47ef-6800-5c53-99fc-6fcc124ca2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430190} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a130d7-695f-5eff-b612-a89637d42af1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8e47ef-6800-5c53-99fc-6fcc124ca2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430190} :answer-field/id #uuid "756361aa-d5cf-55f5-9c74-7d766195b840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f501796-fc0b-5879-8eb1-568ded583cc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-175518" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-7<-9$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & <-9 \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-2).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{(-\\infty ,-2)} \\\\  & =[-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7943a26b-d4fa-5ce1-bc47-5ea4873fc367" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed Using Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b5f8c2-2b99-5562-891b-303dd931bed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430181} {:answer/id #uuid "4277be64-1b71-5d62-a369-59d7b2d5d193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430185} {:answer/id #uuid "4c605d05-6b7a-5db3-b1e6-f476658f16d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430186} {:answer/id #uuid "a428c3b8-01de-5e8f-b73b-74fada2e9234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430191} {:answer/id #uuid "a48dea4d-1fe6-5b8f-813a-9fa35ad0c35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24b5f8c2-2b99-5562-891b-303dd931bed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430181} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fb1666-ac67-59fa-9a0b-88ff4f949f8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f075ba4-7815-572a-b12a-c4691f9f8fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-176028" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x\\ge y$\n\nThe predicate $P(x,y)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "In plain English, our predicate $P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *smaller than* $y.$ Therefore, $¬P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x<y$"}]}
